{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the use of a porphyrinic metal-organic framework, PCN-222, as a highly efficient and selective heterogeneous photocatalyst for the aerobic oxidative coupling of amines to imines under visible light and ambient conditions. The study provides direct ESR evidence for a linker-to-cluster charge transfer (LCCT) mechanism, where photogenerated electrons in Zr-oxo clusters activate oxygen to superoxide radicals, while holes in the porphyrin motifs activate amines, synergistically promoting the reaction alongside energy transfer-generated singlet oxygen.",
